The woff2 files are Latin subsets of the upstream Adwaita fonts, made with fonttools:

  R="U+0000-017F,U+0218-021B,U+02C6,U+02DA,U+02DC,U+0300-036F,U+2000-206F,U+20AC,U+2122,U+2190-21FF,U+2212,U+FEFF,U+FFFD"
  pyftsubset AdwaitaSans-Regular.woff2 --unicodes="$R" --output-file=sans.ttf
  fonttools varLib.instancer sans.ttf opsz=drop wght=400:700 -o sans-final.ttf
  pyftsubset AdwaitaMono-Regular.woff2 --unicodes="$R" --output-file=mono.ttf
  # then save each as woff2 (fonttools ttLib with flavor="woff2"; needs the brotli module)

Keep the unicode-range in app.css in sync with $R.
